      "hints": [
        "Use $T_4 = ar^3 = 64$ with $a = 216$ to find $r^3 = \\frac{64}{216} = \\frac{8}{27}$.",
        "Deduce $r = \\frac{2}{3}$.",
        "Apply the sum to infinity formula $S_\\infty = \\frac{a}{1 - r}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the common ratio $r$ of the geometric progression using $T_1 = a = 216$ and $T_4 = ar^3 = 64$:\n$$216r^3 = 64 \\implies r^3 = \\frac{64}{216} = \\frac{8}{27} \\implies r = \\frac{2}{3}$$",
        "Calculate the sum to infinity using $S_\\infty = \\frac{a}{1 - r}$ (valid since $|r| < 1$):\n$$S_\\infty = \\frac{216}{1 - \\frac{2}{3}} = \\frac{216}{\\frac{1}{3}} = 216 \\times 3 = 648$$"
      ],
