      "hints": [
        "Find GP terms $T_2 = 216\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) = 144$ and $T_3 = 216\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2 = 96$.",
        "Set up AP equations: $u_2 = a + d = 144$ and $u_5 = a + 4d = 96$.",
        "Solve simultaneously to find $a = 160$ and $d = -16$.",
        "Calculate the sum $S_{21} = \\frac{21}{2}[2a + 20d]$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the second and third terms of the geometric progression:\n$$T_2 = 216 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 144$$\n$$T_3 = 216 \\times \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2 = 96$$",
        "Equate to the corresponding arithmetic progression terms:\n$$u_2 = a + d = 144$$\n$$u_5 = a + 4d = 96$$",
        "Subtract the two simultaneous equations to solve for $d$ and $a$:\n$$(a + 4d) - (a + d) = 96 - 144 \\implies 3d = -48 \\implies d = -16$$\n$$a = 144 - (-16) = 160$$",
        "Calculate the sum of the first $21$ terms using $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}[2a + (n - 1)d]$:\n$$S_{21} = \\frac{21}{2}[2(160) + 20(-16)] = \\frac{21}{2}[320 - 320] = \\frac{21}{2}(0) = 0$$"
